userStories.description:
**Goal** — Define `statefulDebaterOp` in `src/operations/debate-stateful.ts`, create `raceAgainstAbort` in `src/debate/utils.ts`, and rewrite `runStateful` in `src/debate/runner-stateful.ts` as a coordinator that dispatches N parallel `callOp` invocations with `hopBody`-managed per-debater session state.

**Motivation** — `runner-stateful.ts` directly calls `sessionManager.openSession` / `agentManager.runAsSession` — the Layer-3/2 escape hatch sanctioned only as a stopgap. Issue #855 tracks removal; each direct session call duplicates tier-label → ModelDef resolution that vanishes once dispatch goes through `callOp`.

**Approach** — Coordinator-over-`hopBody` pattern: `RunOperation.hopBody` runs inside a single session opened by `callOp` (`build-hop-callback.ts:214-282`). The session opens before `hopBody` runs and closes in `finally`. Between `ctx.send(...)` turns, the body can `await` arbitrary promises (cross-debater barriers) and the session stays warm — preserving working-memory semantics that current stateful debate relies on (each debater sees its own prior turns when generating round 1).

Runner = coordinator. Owns N parallel `Promise.withResolvers<string>()` barriers; launches N parallel `callOp(callContext, statefulDebaterOp, input)` invocations bounded by `maxConcurrentDebaters`; aggregates proposal text from settled proposal barriers and rebuttal text from the op return values. Concurrency bound read from `ctx.callContext.runtime.configLoader.current().debate?.maxConcurrentDebaters ?? 2` (full config, not the slice).

Op = per-debater state machine. `hopBody` does: send propose → resolve `proposalBarriers[index]` → `await Promise.all(proposalBarriers)` raced against abort → send rebut. Every barrier `await` uses:
```typescript
const peers = await raceAgainstAbort(
  Promise.all(ctx.input.proposalBarriers.map((b) => b.promise)),
  ctx.input.signal,
  ctx.input.storyId,
);
```

Failure discipline: when any `callOp` invocation throws (abort / no-output) OR returns a result with `success: false`, coordinator rejects all unresolved peer `proposalBarriers` — prevents peer deadlock. Coordinator detects silent agent failure via a `success: boolean` discriminant on the op output type without relying exclusively on `callOp` throwing.

Cost: `callOp` run-kind does not surface `estimatedCostUsd` in parsed output `O`. Coordinator sets `cost: 0` per debater op result (interim, tracked in #1036).

**Interface** (updated for actual `callOp` semantics):
```typescript
// src/operations/debate-stateful.ts

export interface DebateStatefulInput {
  readonly debater: Debater;
  readonly index: number;
  readonly proposePrompt: string;
  readonly buildRebutPrompt: (peerProposals: string[]) => string;
  readonly proposalBarriers: PromiseWithResolvers<string>[];
  readonly signal: AbortSignal;
  readonly storyId: string;
}

export interface DebateStatefulOutput {
  readonly success: boolean;
  readonly rebut: string;
}

export const statefulDebaterOp: RunOperation<DebateStatefulInput, DebateStatefulOutput, DebateConfig> = {
  kind: "run",
  name: "debate-stateful",
  stage: "review",
  session: { role: "debate-stateful" satisfies SessionRole, lifetime: "fresh" },
  config: debateConfigSelector,
  model: (input) => ({ agent: input.debater.agent, model: input.debater.model ?? "fast" }),
  hopBody: async (initial, ctx) => {
    const proposal = await ctx.send(initial);
    ctx.input.proposalBarriers[ctx.input.index].resolve(proposal.output);
    const peers = await raceAgainstAbort(
      Promise.all(ctx.input.proposalBarriers.map((b) => b.promise)),
      ctx.input.signal,
      ctx.input.storyId,
    );
    return ctx.send(ctx.input.buildRebutPrompt(peers));
  },
  build(input, _ctx) {
    return { role: { id: "role", content: "", overridable: false }, task: { id: "task", content: input.proposePrompt, overridable: false } };
  },
  parse(output, _input, _ctx) {
    return { success: !output.startsWith('Agent "'), rebut: output };
  },
};
```

Note on `parse`: it receives only the final turn's output (per `callOp` semantics) and must stay synchronous/side-effect-free. Proposal text therefore remains coordinator-owned data read back from the resolved barriers after the run completes; the op output must not pretend to contain a synchronous `proposal` field unless it actually has one.

`raceAgainstAbort<T>` goes in `src/debate/utils.ts` (new file), re-exported from `src/debate/index.ts`. Signature: `(promise: Promise<T>, signal: AbortSignal, storyId: string | undefined) => Promise<T>`. Throws `NaxError` with code `"CALL_OP_ABORTED"` when `signal.aborted` is true; otherwise resolves with the promise value.

Prompt building: `runStateful`'s coordinator builds `proposePrompt` and rebuttal prompts via `DebatePromptBuilder` — no multi-line prompt strings assembled inline.

**Scope** — In: `src/operations/debate-stateful.ts` (create), `src/debate/utils.ts` (create), `src/debate/runner-stateful.ts` (rewrite coordinator), `src/operations/index.ts` (add export). Out: hybrid/plan runners, US-006 helper deletions, verifier-pick refactor.

**Goal** — Define `hybridDebaterOp` in `src/operations/debate-hybrid.ts` and rewrite `runHybrid` in `src/debate/runner-hybrid.ts` as a coordinator using the same `callOp`/barrier pattern established in US-003.

**Motivation** — `runner-hybrid.ts` directly calls `sessionManager.openSession` / `agentManager.runAsSession` — the Layer-3/2 escape hatch. It also has dual handle ownership logic (`internalHandles` vs. caller-provided handles) that is eliminated once session lifecycle moves into `hopBody`.

**Approach** — `hybridDebaterOp` differs from `statefulDebaterOp` only in the rebut-round semantics: hybrid debate runs N rounds of rebuttals with per-round barriers, rather than a single rebut turn. The output type mirrors the stateful op, and proposal text remains coordinator-owned barrier data just as in US-003.

The rebuttal-loop ordering must avoid round-start deadlock. Each round therefore uses the prior round's settled peer outputs to build the next prompt, then resolves the current round's slot after its own send succeeds. For round 1, the prior material is the proposal barrier set. For later rounds, the prior material is the previous rebuttal round's barrier set. One valid shape is:
```typescript
// src/operations/debate-hybrid.ts
export interface DebateHybridOutput {
  readonly success: boolean;
  readonly rebut: string;  // final round's rebuttal output
}

// inside hybridDebaterOp.hopBody:
let priorPeerOutputs = await raceAgainstAbort(
  Promise.all(ctx.input.proposalBarriers.map((b) => b.promise)),
  ctx.input.signal,
  ctx.input.storyId,
);
for (let round = 1; round <= rounds; round++) {
  const myRebut = await ctx.send(ctx.input.buildRebutPrompt(round, priorPeerOutputs));
  ctx.input.rebutBarriers[round - 1][ctx.input.index].resolve(myRebut.output);
  if (round < rounds) {
    priorPeerOutputs = await raceAgainstAbort(
      Promise.all(ctx.input.rebutBarriers[round - 1].map((b) => b.promise)),
      ctx.input.signal,
      ctx.input.storyId,
    );
  }
}
```

The op fields mirror `statefulDebaterOp`:
```typescript
export const hybridDebaterOp: RunOperation<DebateHybridInput, DebateHybridOutput, DebateConfig> = {
  kind: "run",
  name: "debate-hybrid",
  stage: "review",
  session: { role: "debate-hybrid" satisfies SessionRole, lifetime: "fresh" },
  config: debateConfigSelector,
  model: (input) => ({ agent: input.debater.agent, model: input.debater.model ?? "fast" }),
  // hopBody: multi-round rebuttal loop (see above)
  // build: same pattern as statefulDebaterOp
  // parse: same success discriminant as statefulDebaterOp
};
```

`runHybrid` coordinator: builds per-debater `DebateHybridInput` with proposal barriers (round 0) and per-round rebuttal barriers (`rebutBarriers[round][debaterIndex]`). Launches N parallel `callOp(ctx.callContext, hybridDebaterOp, input)`. When any invocation throws OR returns `success: false`, rejects all unresolved barriers across ALL rounds — not just the current round.

Prompt building: coordinator builds prompts via `DebatePromptBuilder` — no multi-line prompt strings assembled inline.

Reuses `raceAgainstAbort` from `src/debate/utils.ts` (created in US-003).

**Scope** — In: `src/operations/debate-hybrid.ts` (create), `src/debate/runner-hybrid.ts` (rewrite), `src/operations/index.ts` (add export), `runRebuttalLoop` helper deletion as part of runner rewrite. Out: plan runner, US-006 deletions.

**Goal** — Define `planDebaterOp` in `src/operations/debate-plan.ts`, rewrite `runPlan` and `runner-plan-helpers.ts` as a coordinator, and refactor `verifier-pick.ts` `runPatchStep` to return a patch prompt to the coordinator (removing the direct `agentManager.runAsSession` call and the `SuccessfulProposal.handle` requirement).

**Motivation** — `runner-plan.ts` directly calls `sessionManager.openSession` / `agentManager.runAsSession` via two divergent code paths (stateful and one-shot). `verifier-pick.ts` `runPatchStep` also calls `agentManager.runAsSession` directly and throws `VERIFIER_PICK_NO_HANDLE` when `SuccessfulProposal.handle` is absent — coupling the selector to session semantics that belong in the runner.

**Approach** — `planDebaterOp` extends the stateful pattern with a coordinator-owned patch decision signal, but the coordinator must not block scoring on full `callOp` completion. Because `callOp` only resolves after `hopBody` returns, `runPlan` needs a second synchronization point for the proposal+rebut stage: the op resolves proposal barriers as in US-003 and additionally resolves a per-debater `rebuttalBarrier` (or equivalent coordinator-owned completion signal) immediately after the rebut turn succeeds and before awaiting the patch decision. The coordinator scores once all rebuttal-stage signals settle, then resolves all patch-decision signals: winner gets `{ patchPrompt }` when patch is enabled and runner-up overlap < threshold, losers get `{}`.

Updated output type and hopBody sketch:
```typescript
// src/operations/debate-plan.ts
export interface DebatePlanOutput {
  readonly success: boolean;
  readonly rebut: string;
  readonly patched?: string;  // set when the patch turn ran successfully
}

// inside planDebaterOp.hopBody, after the rebut turn:
ctx.input.rebuttalBarrier.resolve(rebutResult.output);
const decision = await raceAgainstAbort(input.selectionSignal, input.signal, input.storyId);
if (decision.patchPrompt) {
  const patched = await ctx.send(decision.patchPrompt);
  return patched;
}
return rebutResult;
```

Op registration (verbatim from spec, adjusted for the extra barrier):
```typescript
export const planDebaterOp: RunOperation<DebatePlanInput, DebatePlanOutput, DebateConfig> = {
  kind: "run",
  name: "debate-plan",
  stage: "plan",
  session: { role: "debate-plan" satisfies SessionRole, lifetime: "fresh" },
  config: debateConfigSelector,
  model: (input) => ({ agent: input.debater.agent, model: input.debater.model ?? "fast" }),
  // hopBody: propose → resolve proposal barrier → await peers → rebut → resolve rebuttalBarrier → await selectionSignal → optional patch
};
```

`runPlan` coordinator:
1. Constructs N `PromiseWithResolvers<{ patchPrompt?: string }>` (one `selectionSignal` per debater).
2. Constructs N coordinator-owned `PromiseWithResolvers<string>` rebuttal-stage barriers (or equivalent signal objects) that carry the pre-patch rebuttal outputs needed for scoring and fallback.
3. Launches N parallel `callOp(ctx.callContext, planDebaterOp, input)` with proposal barriers, rebuttal-stage barriers, and the `selectionSignal` promise.
4. Waits for all debaters to complete proposal + rebut turns by awaiting the rebuttal-stage barriers, not by awaiting full `callOp` completion.
5. Runs scoring by delegating to existing verifier-pick scoring helpers (`extractManifestFromContext`, `computeScore`, `acOverlap`).
6. When patch is enabled in `stageConfig.selector` (kind `"verifier-pick"`) and runner-up overlap < `overlapThreshold`: builds patch prompt (by calling refactored `runPatchStep` which now returns a prompt string, not dispatches to an agent), resolves the winner's signal with `{ patchPrompt }`, resolves losers' signals with `{}`.
7. When patch is disabled or overlap >= threshold: resolves all signals with `{}`.
8. After patch decisions are released, awaits full `callOp` completion and assembles the final `DebateResult`, preserving existing pre-debate phase, selector behavior, hybrid/stateful plan behavior, and post-debate verifier flows.

`runPatchStep` in `verifier-pick.ts` is reduced to: build the patch prompt from `winner.proposal.output` + deltas, return it to the coordinator. The `verifierPickSelector` internal patch block is removed, so selector-level code no longer dispatches patch turns directly. It no longer calls `agentManager.runAsSession`. The `handle?: SessionHandle` field on `SuccessfulProposal` is no longer needed and is removed.

`runner-plan-helpers.ts` session lifecycle helpers become dead code under the coordinator pattern and are removed explicitly: `openPlanSessions`, `closePlanSessions`, `runStatefulPlanTurn`, and `makeStatefulProposal`.

Patch turn failure: if the winner's patch `ctx.send` fails, the runner returns the pre-patch rebuttal output captured from the rebuttal-stage barrier (no behavior regression vs. today's `try/catch` at `verifier-pick.ts:167-179`).

Prompt building: coordinator builds proposal and rebuttal prompts via `DebatePromptBuilder` — no multi-line prompt strings assembled inline.

**Scope** — In: `src/operations/debate-plan.ts` (create), `src/debate/runner-plan.ts` (rewrite), `src/debate/runner-plan-helpers.ts` (remove `openPlanSessions`, `closePlanSessions`, `runStatefulPlanTurn`, `makeStatefulProposal`), `src/debate/selectors/verifier-pick.ts` (remove selector-level patch dispatch block and return prompt string from `runPatchStep`), `src/debate/session-helpers.ts` (remove handle field from SuccessfulProposal), `src/operations/index.ts` (add export). Out: US-006 helper deletions (resolveDebaterModel etc.), selector slim.
